00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:43.740
So at Google, we try to make the
entire data lifecycle simple.

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:48.050
So we have tools and
services across these four

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:49.940
fundamental lines.

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:54.800
The first one, of course,
being the ingestion.

00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:56.270
There were days
wherein people used

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:59.730
to kind of keep batch ingesting
a lot of data-- like once

00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:00.230
in an hour.

00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:02.600
You know, your data
[INAUDIBLE] once in a day,

00:05:02.600 --> 00:05:05.180
and then you have a lot
of analytics and reporting

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:06.570
running on top of it.

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:09.680
But the way streaming
analytics has

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:11.690
grown over the
past few years, it

00:05:11.690 --> 00:05:14.540
has become one of the
most critical components

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:16.280
of most of the businesses.

00:05:16.280 --> 00:05:20.310
So if you have to
stream ingest your data,

00:05:20.310 --> 00:05:24.020
you can use Pub/Sub, which
is our messaging bus at GCP.

00:05:24.020 --> 00:05:26.960
But if you come from Kafka, or
any other messaging background,

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:29.420
you can use that as well.

00:05:29.420 --> 00:05:34.550
From a data pipeline and
processing perspective,

00:05:34.550 --> 00:05:38.780
we have Cloud Dataflow on
which you can run Apache Beam.

00:05:38.780 --> 00:05:41.060
I'm sure you might
have gone through some

00:05:41.060 --> 00:05:43.190
of the sessions in
the last two days

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:45.350
on Dataflow and Apache Beam.

00:05:45.350 --> 00:05:48.470
And if you're coming from the
Hadoop or Spark background,

00:05:48.470 --> 00:05:51.170
you can run it on top
of Cloud Dataproc.

00:05:51.170 --> 00:05:53.960
When it comes to
building your data lake

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:56.830
or building your
data warehouse, you

00:05:56.830 --> 00:06:00.230
have two options, which is
BigQuery and cloud storage.

00:06:00.230 --> 00:06:03.986
Again, choosing whether to
have your data lake in BigQuery

00:06:03.986 --> 00:06:06.350
or cloud storage,
you know, there

00:06:06.350 --> 00:06:09.750
are some pros and
cons on that as well.

00:06:09.750 --> 00:06:11.970
And, of course, at the end
is the advanced analytics.

00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:16.190
So once you land your data
either in BigQuery or cloud

00:06:16.190 --> 00:06:19.130
storage, you can run all
of your advanced analytics,

00:06:19.130 --> 00:06:23.070
your machine learning, your
reporting, and whatnot.

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:27.640
So as I was saying,
streaming analytics

00:06:27.640 --> 00:06:31.520
has gained a lot of importance
over the past few years.

00:06:31.520 --> 00:06:33.550
So this is one of the
most common patterns which

00:06:33.550 --> 00:06:37.240
we see most of the customers
using wherein you have

00:06:37.240 --> 00:06:39.950
your devices, you have
your applications-- web,

00:06:39.950 --> 00:06:41.630
mobile, whatnot.

00:06:41.630 --> 00:06:44.590
And then you bring a
messaging bus in between.

00:06:44.590 --> 00:06:47.260
You get to choose
between Pub/Sub, Kafka,

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:49.360
or any other messaging bus.

00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:51.760
And then you use
Apache Beam on top

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:54.040
of Dataflow for transformation.

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:58.600
Or you use Spark or
any other open source

00:06:58.600 --> 00:07:00.790
component on Dataproc.

00:07:00.790 --> 00:07:03.010
And then you have an
option to land the data

00:07:03.010 --> 00:07:04.990
across multiple storage systems.

00:07:04.990 --> 00:07:09.730
So BigQuery is the most popular
choice when you have analytics,

00:07:09.730 --> 00:07:13.540
